nts-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:dab38465be18969f88075861510d6c74a42f359d1207e243dc26a75ec3b3a375","file":"preprints/Relative-independence-of-the-separable-quotient-problem-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":34,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"2c14cca0796a2080c2089628a1dcfc99fd1e3e7953f0aa1e80a0d32b625215d4","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Relative-independence-of-the-separable-quotient-problem-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:dab38465be18969f88075861510d6c74a42f359d1207e243dc26a75ec3b3a375","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Relative-independence-of-the-separable-quotient-problem-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L34"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{intro:main}\nFor each $\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\R,\\C\\}$, ZFC proves the following implications.\n\\begin{enumerate}[label=\\textup{(\\roman*)}]\n \\item If $\\mathfrak c$ is real-valued measurable, then $\\SQ_{\\mathbb F}$\n holds.\n \\item If the continuum hypothesis holds, then $\\SQ_{\\mathbb F}$ fails.\n\\end{enumerate}\nConsequently, if ZFC with a measurable cardinal is consistent, then\n$\\SQ_{\\mathbb F}$ is independent of ZFC. Consistency of its failure\nrequires only consistency of ZFC."}
